Pi (coding agent)
Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
Licensed under the MIT License
https://github.com/earendil-works/pi  (commit ede2c9b)

The following modules contain code or mechanisms derived from Pi:

  core/src/agent/compact.rs   — token-budget compaction boundaries
                                (keepRecentTokens), the rule that a kept tail
                                never starts on a tool result
  core/src/agent/context.rs   — keep_tail_boundary
  core/src/agent/cache_warmer.rs
                              — cache warmer scheduling and eligibility (TTL
                                ratio, savings floor, replayability)

Modifications made:
  - rewritten in Rust for Meridian's ChatMessage and SeaORM models
  - the compaction anchor is a database row id, not a JSONL entry id; summaries
    are side rows (is_compact_summary) rather than appended entries
  - the token estimate uses Meridian's TokenCounter where one is available,
    and Pi's characters/4 estimate only where the model is not yet resolved
  - the warmer implements the streaming lifecycle only (no idle mode), uses
    Meridian's ChatProvider and audit ledger, and takes its rates from the
    model configuration the turn already priced itself with

